{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-beta-bar-even-kernel-invariant","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:q-beta-bar-even-kernel-invariant","kind":"proposition","title":"$\\mathfrak{Q}_\\beta$ precision-ladder $\\bar{}$-even discriminant — the kernel $R(q,\\xi)$ produces a clean integer-$u$ ladder $\\prod_k(1+c_k\\,u^k)$ if and only if $R$ is even under $t \\mapsto -t$ ($t = q-1$); $(1-u^2)$ at N=2 is the prototype","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-beta-c-2-eq-neg-one-structural","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference"],"cites":["references/jones1987","references/wenzl1988","references/habiro2004"],"tags":["q-beta","precision-ladder","structural","bar-involution","kernel-invariant","no-fit","formalize-first"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenInvariant.bar_even_quadratic_term_in_t_squared","text":"q-beta-bar-even-kernel-invariant.md","leanSource":"q-beta-bar-even-kernel-invariant.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:q-beta-bar-even-kernel-invariant\"></a><p><em>In the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{Q}_\\beta</code> ladder</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  R(u) := \\prod_k(1 + c_k u^k), \\qquad u = b(q) \\cdot \\hbar_q^2,</code></pre>\n<p><em>the ladder admits a clean integer-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u</code> Taylor representation if and only if <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> is bar-even (an even function of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">t := q - 1</code> about <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code>).</em></p>\n<p>The substrate variable <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u</code> has a double zero at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code>. Under <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\mapsto q^{-1}</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">t \\mapsto -t + O(t^2)</code>. If <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> is even in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">t</code>, the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u</code>-grading absorbs the coefficients, avoiding a <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sqrt{u}</code> branch. If <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> has odd-in-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">t</code> content, the reversion picks up a <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sqrt{u}</code> branch, making the scalar extraction singular.</p>\n<p>This is the formalize-first gate for the bar-even invariant. The candidate is a power series in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">t</code>. Compute <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R(q^{-1}, \\xi^{-1})</code> and subtract. A non-zero difference refutes the candidate structurally.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-invariant.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.9.14","page":"b/prop-q-beta-bar-even-kernel-invariant","qa":{"counts":{"pass":87,"fail":2,"warn":1,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":75},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Nuclear.QBeta.BarEvenInvariant.bar_even_quadratic_term_in_t_squared","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-invariant.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
